## MQClientInstance scheduled-executor caller API — 2026-10-23T03:57:38Z

Pinned source audit confirmed that `MQClientInstance.getScheduledExecutorService()` returns the same single-thread executor used by its periodic client callbacks. `PullMessageService` has a separate executor and a separate getter. Rust now exposes `ClientRuntime::scheduled_executor_service() -> RuntimeScheduler` for immediate/delayed async work, fixed-rate/fixed-delay callbacks, per-task cancellation, and runtime-owned shutdown. The public handle uses the owned client scheduler and accepts work before runtime start.

Code revision: `5c808754` (`feat(runtime): expose client task scheduler handle`). Validation passed: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-core --lib` (218 tests), `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-core --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`, `cargo fmt --all`, and `git diff --check`. The new paused-time test covers pre-start work, one-shot delay, both repeating modes, cancellation, and shutdown.

The row remains partial: Java's result-bearing `Future` and executor-wide lifecycle APIs are not yet exposed, and the separate `PullMessageService.getScheduledExecutorService()` handle remains unmapped. Broad P18-V01 source/API/settings/input/error/control-flow and reverse-export reconciliation, current-revision remote Ubuntu CI, native Windows execution, and Phase 19 Broker/Docker validation remain open. No remote CI, push, Broker, or Docker action was performed; protected Phase 19 worktree files remain unchanged and unstaged.

## PullMessageService scheduled-executor getter — 2026-10-23T04:02:31Z

Pinned source confirms a second, independent `ScheduledExecutorService` owned by `PullMessageService`. Code revision `2c52ac4d` adds `ClientRuntime::pull_scheduled_executor_service() -> RuntimeScheduler`, routed through the pull service's own scheduled queue. The handle supports immediate/delayed async work, fixed-rate/fixed-delay callbacks, per-task cancellation, and the PullMessageService shutdown path. Its pre-start regression verifies delayed execution and prompt queue removal after cancellation.

Validation passed on `2c52ac4d`: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-core --lib` (219 tests), `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-core --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`, `cargo fmt --all`, and `git diff --check`. The executor-wide Java methods, result-bearing `Future`, and inherited thread controls remain unmapped, so both scheduler rows remain partial under P18-V01. Broad Java source/API/settings/input/error/control-flow and Rust reverse-export reconciliation, remote Ubuntu CI, native Windows execution, and Phase 19 Broker/Docker validation remain open. No external actions were run, and the four protected Phase 19 paths remain unchanged and unstaged.

