## Scheduled-executor lifecycle controls — 2026-10-23T04:19:56Z

Pinned Java `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9` confirms the client and PullMessageService getters return distinct `ScheduledExecutorService` instances. Commit `4c337b1e` adds Rust lifecycle controls to both `RuntimeScheduler` handles: graceful and immediate shutdown, shutdown/termination status, and async termination wait. Graceful shutdown retains queued one-shots while ending periodic registrations; immediate shutdown drops queued work, signals cancellation to the active Rust future, and reports the pending queue size without self-joining. Pull scheduler shutdown is independent from immediate FIFO pull dispatch. Regressions cover both owners, status/wait timeout and transitions, returned/cancelled work, full runtime shutdown, and worker-initiated immediate shutdown.

Validation on `4c337b1e`: `cargo test --offline -p rocketmq-classic-core --lib --locked` (227 passed), `cargo clippy --offline -p rocketmq-classic-core --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`, `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, and `git diff --check` passed. `docs/compatibility/PHASE_6_API_CONFIG_MAP.md`, `docs/compatibility/PHASE_6_RUNTIME_INVENTORY.md`, and `docs/release-checklist.md` record the scheduler closure. Broad P18-V01 source/API/settings/input/error/control-flow and reverse-export reconciliation, current-revision remote Ubuntu CI, native Windows execution, and Phase 19 Broker/Docker validation remain open. No remote CI, push, Broker, or Docker action was performed; the four Phase 19 user-owned worktree paths remain untouched.

