## ExecutorService bulk invocation mapping — 2026-10-23T04:42:34Z

Pinned Java `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9` returns
`ScheduledExecutorService` from both runtime scheduler getters, inheriting
`ExecutorService.invokeAll` and `invokeAny`. Code revisions `6a960144` and
`e5bbe8df` add Rust async `RuntimeScheduler::invoke_all` and `invoke_any` for
both the client and pull owners. `invoke_all` returns each callback value or
oneshot receive error in submission order. `invoke_any` continues after
panics, returns the first normal task value, and prevents later queued
callbacks from beginning after that value is produced. Empty input and input
where no callback returns a value use explicit `RuntimeError` variants;
dropping the bulk-call future cancels accepted tasks. A Tokio timeout supplies
the Rust caller deadline; Java's timed `invokeAll` partial-future-list result
is not represented as such.

Current Core validation passed on `e5bbe8df`: `cargo test --offline -p
rocketmq-classic-core --lib --locked` (230 tests), all 23
`runtime::tasks::tests`, strict all-target/all-feature Core Clippy,
`cargo fmt --all -- --check`, and `git diff --check`. Broad P18-V01
bidirectional source/API/settings/input/error/control-flow/reverse-export
reconciliation remains open, as do current-revision remote Ubuntu CI, native
Windows runtime execution, and Phase 19 Broker/Docker validation. No external
CI, push, Broker, or Docker action was performed; the four protected Phase 19
worktree paths remain unchanged and unstaged.

## Timed ExecutorService calls and ScheduledFuture waits — 2026-10-23T04:54:53Z

Code revision `c0cb787b` adds timed `invoke_all_with_timeout` and
`invoke_any_with_timeout` to both `RuntimeScheduler` owners, plus per-task
cancelled/finished status, remaining-delay inspection, async wait and
wait-with-timeout methods. `RuntimeScheduledCall` also supports cancellation
status and repeatable result waits with deadlines. The async equivalents retain
completed timed-invoke-all values and identify callback failures and deadline
cancellations; timed invoke-any reports `RuntimeError::InvocationTimeout` and
cancels accepted tasks. Callback panics now have a distinct handle failure
state from cancellation.

